        rows: [
          ['Eccentrocytes (Hemighosts)', 'Asymmetric cell with hemoglobin squeezed to one side; clear crescentic zone of membrane fusion', 'Oxidant cross-linking of membrane skeletal proteins (spectrin) causing collapse and inner adhesion', 'Onion/garlic ingestion (dogs, cats, cattle), red maple leaf (horses), copper (sheep), zinc, Brassica, mothballs'],
          ['Heinz bodies', 'Pale refractile blebs on Romanowsky stain; bright blue round inclusions on New Methylene Blue stain', 'Oxidation of globin sulfhydryl (-SH) groups causing hemoglobin denaturation and precipitation on membrane', 'Acetaminophen in cats, onions/garlic, copper poisoning in sheep, red maple toxicity in horses, propylene glycol']
        ]
